## 5. Toolchain parity — FAILED (environment finding)

```text
$ node scripts/version-parity.mjs
toolchain: cannot read pnpm.cmd version: Command failed: pnpm.cmd --version
'pnpm.cmd' is not recognized as an internal or external command,
operable program or batch file.
```

```text
$ pnpm -v
pnpm : The term 'pnpm' is not recognized ...
$ mise --version
mise : The term 'mise' is not recognized ...
$ node -v
v26.13.0
```

`.mise.toml` pins `node = "22"` and `npm:pnpm = "10.34.9"`. Neither is available on PATH in this
session; the shims directory exists (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\mise\shims`) but the `mise` executable is
missing, so the shims cannot resolve a version. The global Node on PATH is 26.13.0.

**Consequence.** Local `pnpm`-based parity cannot be claimed for this task. CI on Linux, which
uses the pinned Node 22 / pnpm 10.34.9, remains the reference environment. This is recorded as
residual risk R-P1 and must be restored before any EP-01 item that needs a local build.

---

## 6. Toolchain parity — RESTORED (2026-11-07)

Root cause: `mise.exe` was present at `%LOCALAPPDATA%\mise\bin\mise.exe`, but that directory was not
on the process `PATH`; the shims could not locate `mise`, so `node` and `pnpm` fell through to the
global Node 26. The binary was never missing.

Fix applied (user environment, no repository change):

```text
$ [Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable('Path', "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\mise\shims;$cur", 'User')
added: C:\Users\HP\AppData\Local\mise\shims
```

`%LOCALAPPDATA%\mise\bin` was already a User `PATH` entry; `shims` was not. Both are now present.

```text
$ node -v
v22.23.4
$ pnpm -v
10.34.9
$ node scripts/version-parity.mjs
toolchain: OK — node 22.23.4, pnpm 10.34.9
toolchain: contract node >=22.0.0 <23, pnpm 10.34.9
```

`pnpm` scripts now run through the pinned toolchain. Full gate suite:

```text
$ pnpm verify
toolchain: OK — node 22.23.4, pnpm 10.34.9
lint: OK — 20 known baseline violation(s), 0 new; 0 stale
Test Files  2 passed (2)
     Tests  18 passed (18)
All push-protection checks passed.
built in 8.52s
exit=0
```

**Consequence.** R-P1 is resolved on this workstation. The run above is the first `pnpm`-native gate
run for this record; earlier sections invoked the underlying Node entry points directly and are kept
unchanged as history. CI on Linux remains the shared reference environment.

